  "text_sanskrit": "नमः पुरस्तादथ पृष्ठतस्ते नमोऽस्तु ते सर्वत एव सर्व । अनन्तवीर्यामितविक्रमस्त्वं सर्वं समाप्नोषि ततोऽसि सर्वः ॥ ११-४० ॥",
  "itrans": "namaH purastAdatha pR^iShThataste namo.astu te sarvata eva sarva . anantavIryAmitavikramastva.n sarva.n samApnoShi tato.asi sarvaH .. 11-40 ..",
  "translation": "Bow to Thee before and behind; and bow to Thee on all sides, O Perfect One; Thou art infinite force and immeasurable prowess; because Thou pervadest everything, therefore Thou art All. (40.) \nV. The explanation of All in the latter half is necessary to make the preceding statements consistent with regard to the Lord's glories. If the Vedic texts such as “All this indeed is Brahman” be thought contradictory to what has been described, the present verse institutes the rule of interpretation in all such cases. The Supreme Being is All because He compasses all, not because He Is identically All. (40)\nA. Arjuna prays for pardon for his past faults towards the Lord of such glories.",
